# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).


## [Unreleased]

### Added

- `normalize()` returns the canonical form of an address (Gmail, Outlook), for deduplication
- `ValidationPipe` type export
- TSDoc on the public API

### Fixed

- `noDisposableEmailAddresses: false` was ignored (config used `|| true`)
- `excludeDomains` had no effect when `noDisposableEmailAddresses` was `false`
- Domain checks are now case-insensitive and ignore surrounding spaces
- Subdomains of blocked domains are blocked too (`foo.10minutemail.com`)
- Provider routing matches the exact domain, not the first label (`gmail.evil.com` is no longer routed to Gmail)
- `msn.com` was routed to the Outlook provider but rejected by it
- Gmail normalization only rewrites `googlemail.com` in the domain part
- Missing `mohmal` domain

### Changed

- Domain lookups use a `Set` instead of scanning an array
- Plus-tag stripping no longer uses regexes

### Removed

- `noGmailAliases` and `noOutlookAliases` options: they never had any effect. Use `normalize()` to deduplicate aliases. TypeScript users passing them will get a type error.

## [1.0.0] - 2023-02-20

### Added

- List of disposable email domains

### Updated

- DevDependencies

## [0.0.3] - 2022-08-31

### Added

- Initial release